WEBVTT

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.900
Understood.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:10.920
All right.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.260
The day after tomorrow, yes?

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:16.020
No, you can get rid of it all.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:16.980
Yes.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.010
Thank you.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.590
Um, it's me.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.090
Come in.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.000
I'd like you to stamp these.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.800
What?

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.450
This time it's ice cream sales?

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:43.600
Mikaze-san said one of the shopping
district guys requested it.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.690
Our school's not a market
for the shopping district.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.610
I think the students would enjoy ice cream.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.800
You just want to impress Mikaze-san, right?

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.780
Please!

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:03.930
<b>Accepted</b>

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.730
Thanks!

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.680
What's this?

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.040
Real estate sale documents?

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.300
Hey, don't look at those!

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:13.840
Sorry.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:57.960
I see.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.170
They're tearing it down tomorrow.

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:00.990
Yeah.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.680
I liked your house.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.990
We'd go to play there, on the
way home from school.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.830
It's kind of a shame.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:13.050
Yeah. You're losing the
house you grew up in.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.210
It can't be helped.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:18.550
No one lives there, and
they wanted the land.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:22.170
Want someone to go with you
when they tear it down?

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.560
I can go.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.690
It's fine.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:32.820
Spiritualism, originally the practice of speaking
with the dead through séances,

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:36.800
was very popular in the
West in the 19th-century.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.610
Communication now is generally
done via a medium.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:45.490
The ouija board and kokkuri-san are
both examples of spiritualism.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.910
We've covered this in earlier classes, yes?

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.620
And so today, I'm going to summon a spirit.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.590
This time, we're going to have the spirit
materialize through ectoplasm.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.730
Materialize?

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.820
Is it that simple?

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.820
Actually, what's ectoplasm?

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:09.670
It was on the last test, remember?

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:12.450
It's human life energy.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:16.310
When a spirit uses it, you can see - 
or in some cases - touch it.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:20.360
But it's extremely difficult for a
spirit to take material form.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:24.180
The famous 19th-century
medium, Helen Duncan,

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.660
died while attempting to
materialize a spirit.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:33.120
Does anyone have any suggestions
for whom we should summon?

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.930
My granny died last year. How about her?

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.200
Can it be a celebrity?

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.650
Then I'd like to see the pro wrestler...

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.080
I want to see Spot!

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.420
I think we should summon the principal!

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:49.790
He knows everyone here, and I'm a big fan!

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:53.460
What the hell's wrong with you?

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:55.430
Glasses... My glasses...

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.430
Think about Maya!

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:56.560
It's fine, really.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:00.610
It'll make things easier for everyone.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.130
Then turn off the air conditioner.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.990
During the summoning, the
temperature will sink.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:17.990
I summon here the soul of the
Waldstein Academy principal,

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:19.750
Kumashiro Jun'ichiro.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.670
Use my body to come down to this Earth!

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.560
That's not the principal!

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:37.700
I saw it!

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.440
Where am I?

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:50.320
Snow?

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:56.970
Who's this girl?

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.300
Come here.

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:08.110
She's gone.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:09.370
Yeah.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.710
Did you see the principal?

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:24.420
Man, why was it a girl, not the principal?

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.590
It's just that difficult.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:31.230
She must've been on the same
wavelength as the vice-principal.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:32.310
I see.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:33.390
Hey, Maya.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:34.920
What?

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.470
Would you do something with her?

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:39.350
That's that girl.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:43.850
I was out back, working on my bike,
when she just jumped on me.

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:47.010
She won't get off my back.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.360
She's really asleep.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:53.320
Aw, I want to give a ghost
a piggy-back ride.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.850
You can't see it?

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:56.200
Not at all!

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.870
I can!

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.940
Even Kozue?

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:02.370
But I can tell where it is.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.880
Same as always.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.980
Do something.

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.510
Where am I?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:17.140
Where is my home?

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.590
I want to go home!

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:39.020
I'll look for it with you.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.290
Really?

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:44.750
Yeah.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:59.520
Wait...

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:02.360
Where are you?

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:04.100
Okamoto Akari, age seven.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.560
She was a first grader in elementary school.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.580
She appeared during the
spirit-summoning ceremony.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:11.830
So she's a ghost?

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:13.850
She says she wants to go home.

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:18.130
If we knew her elementary school,
we could find her house.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:19.450
We're all going to help her.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:22.910
That's strange.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:24.170
What is?

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:27.830
It's clearly unrelated to Nostradamus's Key,

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:30.210
but you're really getting involved.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:35.170
Even I wouldn't ignore a crying little girl.

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.020
And...

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:41.640
If we find her house, maybe we
can send back her soul.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.890
I'm not doing much.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.990
I can help you after school.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:48.650
Maya?

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:52.480
No, it's nothing.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:56.190
Abe-sensei!

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:00.680
Mikaze-san!

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:06.950
Thank you so much for the
thing with the ice cream!

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.990
I knew I could count on you!

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.170
Oh, no.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:16.630
Um, after school, do you have some time?

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.530
After school?

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:24.180
Um, there's something I'd like to ask you.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:26.780
Um...

00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:29.580
Abe-sensei?

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.770
Yes, fine.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:34.350
Great.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:35.820
See you later.

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:01.010
Why me?

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.590
Your knees are the most stable!

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:04.790
Right?

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:05.990
Right?

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.920
Something happen, Maya?

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.110
No, nothing.

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:27.990
There are six Matsushiro
elementary schools.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:31.830
We could hit them up, one by one,
but that's kind of a pain.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:35.050
What's at your school?

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:39.570
A gate and a yard?

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:40.960
A gate and a yard?

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:42.400
The gate's at the entrance?

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:46.550
Every school's got one of these.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:48.810
Does that mean it's gotta have
a memorable gate and yard?

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:55.360
What's wrong?

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:58.170
Sorry. I just figured it out.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:00.280
Do you think she meant...

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.890
The Sanada Mansion?

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:06.150
I'm pretty sure that next to it...

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:09.240
Thank you.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:12.460
My intuition's brilliant, isn't it?

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:15.220
I guess even you must be useful sometimes.

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:16.400
Shut up!

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:19.420
I'm so glad we found Akari-chan's school.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:22.220
Her teacher was nice.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:25.390
It's about a ten minute walk to her house.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:29.850
Home, home, home, home.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:31.730
She looks happy.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:33.600
She must've really wanted to go home.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:35.330
Home...

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:52.790
Here you go.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.070
Omelet curry?

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:01.020
We're going to add it to our menu.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:03.880
You really like curry, so I thought
I'd ask your opinion.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:06.260
I see...

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:11.390
She was so insistent, I thought it was
a date or something more important.

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:15.320
Let's eat.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:21.120
Well?

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.780
That was delicious.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.610
Thank you.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:28.740
I'm so glad.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:32.800
I wanted you to eat it first.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:34.700
I put my heart into making it.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:48.550
This is it.

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:50.760
Home.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.380
<b>Okamoto</b>

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.400
Home.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:14.620
I'm glad you're home.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:16.860
It's cold.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.000
It's cold.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:27.720
Where am I?

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:38.520
A poltergeist?

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:42.260
It's cold.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:49.400
Watch out!

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.510
What is this?

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:55.270
Didn't she want to go home?

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:58.120
Amazing spirit energy...

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:07.080
Maya! Kozue!

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:10.840
Are you okay?

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.060
For now, let's get out of here!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.000
Kozue, you alive?

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:24.400
Maya...

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:26.780
Hey, Maya!

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:42.700
What's wrong?

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.940
Why do you look so hurt?

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:47.170
What do we do?

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:12.880
Hey!

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:16.070
What are you doing?

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:21.070
It's hard to believe...

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:22.790
Little Akari-chan.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.560
But I believe you.

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:29.960
I know all about the Occult Academy.
My nephew went there.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.900
Oh, eat up. Eat up.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:33.380
Those snacks are good.

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:35.840
Th-thank you.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:40.810
It feels like she might show up,
any minute, just fine.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:45.380
Um, if you don't mind, could you
tell us what happened to her?

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.730
It might help us put her spirit to rest.

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:51.780
She was such a good, cheery girl.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.820
She was always so polite.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:57.270
But she had a sad life.

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:04.250
Just as she entered elementary school,
her parents divorced.

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:08.980
Her father looked after her, but it's hard
for a single man to raise a child.

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:14.300
She must've been lonely,
but she was always smiling.

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:17.430
I'm home, ma'am!

00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:18.730
Welcome back.

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:19.550
You alone again today?

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:21.870
Want to eat at my place?

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:23.830
No, I'm fine.

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:26.090
I can take care of myself!

00:17:26.090 --> 00:17:30.270
As the landlord, I tried to do what I could,

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:34.490
but I didn't think it was my
place to get too involved.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:37.490
And then it happened.

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:38.650
It?

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:43.660
She froze to death on Christmas Eve.

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:48.810
She was sitting in front of the
door the whole snowy night.

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:51.960
Why?

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.810
Why was she sitting outside?

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.830
I don't really know.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:04.350
But when I think of how I didn't
find her sooner, I just...

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:12.270
We need to do something, yeah.

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:16.990
But if her emotions are
that strong, it's hard.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.870
Yeah.

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:21.550
We don't know why it happened.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:24.330
Maya.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:26.030
What's wrong?

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:29.250
Maybe... She, too...

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:33.630
What?

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:40.240
Let's look for a few more clues.

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:43.270
Maybe ask her dad.

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:44.510
There's still more here.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:45.770
Maya.

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:46.890
Right!

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:49.310
Well, I've come this far.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:50.560
That's right.

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:58.130
Hello?

00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.820
Hey, it's me.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:02.320
How'd it go?

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.450
It's going well.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.590
I see.

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:07.090
I'll come meet up now.

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:08.590
It's fine, really.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:12.780
This has nothing to do with the Key.
We don't need you.

00:19:12.780 --> 00:19:14.370
What?

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:15.770
You mad?

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:17.160
No.

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:19.430
See you.

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:20.610
Hey, wait!

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:22.430
Abe-sensei!

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:24.960
Mikaze-san!

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:27.200
You forgot this.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:29.370
Oh, thank you.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.520
I thought I could catch up with you.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:34.670
Hello? Maya?

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:39.290
I'm sorry to interrupt your call...

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:40.530
Not at all.

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.670
Thank you for today.

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:44.620
See you tomorrow.

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:47.980
See you tomorrow...

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.220
Tomorrow?

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:51.850
Who was that?

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:52.580
Abe?

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:53.620
Nah.

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:56.540
Anyway, let's go see her dad.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:20:01.390
But the landlord said she
didn't know his address.

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:04.590
Where did he work, again?

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:06.010
I'm pretty sure it was...

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:07.970
He quit?

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:10.120
Okamoto-san, in sales, right?

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.680
He quit, just after the new year.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:15.590
It hit him hard when his daughter died.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:17.870
Who are you?

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:20.400
His relatives or something?

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:22.900
Actually, Akari-chan's spirit...

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:26.740
Her elementary school teacher asked
us to find out where she was buried.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.020
I see.

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:30.850
Do you have a contact address for him?

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.810
Since he quit, we haven't
spoken to him at all.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:38.600
Actually, one of my co-workers
said he saw him...

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:40.000
Where?

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:45.760
Okamoto-san? You have visitors.

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:54.390
We'd like to talk to you
about your daughter.

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:58.590
During a class on spirit summoning,

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:00.270
her spirit appeared.

00:21:00.270 --> 00:21:03.500
She's still attached to the
place she used to live.

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:08.160
If you don't do something...

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.120
Leave.

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:12.880
I don't care if you're from the
Occult Academy or whatever,

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:14.570
but don't pull this crap on me.

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:15.740
Leave!

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:17.380
You can't mean...

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:18.880
Leave!

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:19.790
Leave!

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:21.600
Leave!

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:28.970
W-Wait!

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:29.790
We're-

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:30.970
You're bothering me.

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:35.600
You don't want to save her?

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.200
Maya...

